  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Congratulations on packaging up all your scenes into a single application that showcases your work as a portfolio project, accessible from a single menu screen.\n\nHere are some of the things you learned how to do along the way:\n\n\u2022 Adjust the display of icons in the <b>Scene</b> view using the <b>Gizmo</b> dropdown and <b>3D Icons</b> slider. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/GizmosMenu.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022 Explain the role of the canvas GameObject in designing a user interface.\n\u2022 Adjust the properties of the <b>TextMeshPro</b> component to edit text and change its appearance.\n\u2022 Arrange windows in the Unity Editor. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/CustomizingYourWorkspace.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022 Open the <b>Build Profiles</b> window. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/build-profiles-reference.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022 Select the scenes of a Unity project to include in a build. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/build-profiles-reference.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022 Open the <b>Player Settings</b> window. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/class-PlayerSettings.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022 Enter the Player Settings that determine how the application is displayed on a target platform. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/class-PlayerSettings.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n"
